    <briefdescription>
<para>Simple deterministic <computeroutput><ref refid="classthemis_1_1prompt__engineering_1_1_i_prompt_a_b_framework" kindref="compound">IPromptABFramework</ref></computeroutput> backed by an in-memory experiment registry. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Variant assignment uses FNV-1a-32 over <computeroutput>user_id + &apos;\0&apos; + key</computeroutput> modulo 100 to decide traffic split, matching the behaviour of <computeroutput><ref refid="classthemis_1_1prompt__engineering_1_1_prompt_a_b_experiment_framework" kindref="compound">PromptABExperimentFramework</ref></computeroutput>.</para>
<para>Thread-safe: <computeroutput><ref refid="classthemis_1_1prompt__engineering_1_1_simple_prompt_a_b_framework_1ac454270e9693c870e49034f78517fc7c" kindref="member">assignVariant()</ref></computeroutput> and <computeroutput><ref refid="classthemis_1_1prompt__engineering_1_1_simple_prompt_a_b_framework_1a50f27a26df372f6d91debddfbc1fee5d" kindref="member">listExperiments()</ref></computeroutput> are safe for concurrent read access. <computeroutput><ref refid="classthemis_1_1prompt__engineering_1_1_simple_prompt_a_b_framework_1adcc5b730bbe3153185d9e23d9d0e34c2" kindref="member">registerExperiment()</ref></computeroutput> and <computeroutput><ref refid="classthemis_1_1prompt__engineering_1_1_simple_prompt_a_b_framework_1a31ab664e07546701bee80bd223f2e8ce" kindref="member">deactivate()</ref></computeroutput> are serialised with a shared mutex. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
